{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons","id":1067714,"title":"Which gods and goddesses do you want added to existing pantheons?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-24T11:42:01-07:00","id":1067714,"title":"Which gods and goddesses do you want added to existing pantheons?","content":"I'm aware it's a little early for this, but since we have seen the write-ups for a few of the pantheons, I think now is as reasonable a time as ever to start this discussion. Now, beyond the obvious troubles with conflation within the Egyptian pantheon, one deity I'd like to see added to the Teotl is Xolotl. He was mentioned twice in the write-ups of other gods, and is just a really interesting deity in general. I mean, just look at the guy. \u200b<a href=\"http://amrock.deviantart.com/art/Xolotl-334675937\" target=\"_blank\">http://amrock.deviantart.com/art/Xolotl-334675937</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:16:56-07:00","id":1067784,"title":"","content":"[screams about Het-Heru and Sekhmet]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T16:47:19-07:00","id":1068121,"title":"","content":"The minors greeks gods (nike, hypno, morpheo etcetc) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T22:22:28-07:00","id":1068185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1068121#post1068121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The minors greeks gods (nike, hypno, morpheo etcetc) </div> </div> </div> </div>That reminde me: I'd love to see Cybele/Magna Mater, both for her interesting divine aspects and to see where she (as an Anatolian goddess imported from Greece and to Rome from there) would be sorted Pantheon-wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T11:14:46-07:00","id":1068349,"title":"","content":"Nephthys- I really like her, and she is always mentioned besides the great gods of Egypt, so she is undoubtedly at the top of my list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T16:41:42-07:00","id":1068471,"title":"","content":"I forget, is Hesta listed in the Greek one? She's always been my hands down favorite of the pantheon for some odd reason. Maybe because she's the only one who doesn't act like a jerk.<br /> <br /> Also, Iris, Hebe and Hecate. <br /> <br /> The Loa Loco and Ayizan (he of healing and plants, she of commerce and the marketplace)<br /> <br /> Tsukuyomi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T23:33:28-07:00","id":1068561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1068471#post1068471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget, is Hesta listed in the Greek one? She's always been my hands down favorite of the pantheon for some odd reason. Maybe because she's the only one who doesn't act like a jerk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, Hestia's listed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T08:16:02-07:00","id":1068679,"title":"","content":"Tlazolteotl for the Aztecs. Nephthys for the Egyptians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:00:54-07:00","id":1070641,"title":"","content":"Personally I would like Eros, if only because I find the idea of the god of love being seen as one of the most terrifying things in all of the greek world. And to be fair, how many Tragedies can be traced back to Eros and his bow? Just about all of them. Plus I always loved the story where Ares mocked Eros for having a small javelin instead of a great spear like his, and when Eros asked Ares to hold the Javelin, it slammed his hand against the ground and he was pinned their for some days as Eros wondered off chuckling. I just think Eros is a cool god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T09:28:29-07:00","id":1070696,"title":"","content":"Wasn't the Greek signature character from 1st ed kind of-sort of meant to invoke Eros? For some reason I always had that impression. <br /> <br /> Eris and Harmonia would also be interesting additions to the Greeks. As would Adrestia (either as a stand alone or as part of Nemesis). <br /> <br /> Wadjet, Serket, Neith and Shezmu for the Egyptians. <br /> <br /> And for the Japanese, Tenjin, Kagu-tsuchi and Seidai Myojin (who is the god of sports, which is quite frankly awesome)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T14:47:24-07:00","id":1079520,"title":"","content":"For the Greeks, Demeter, Hecate, Hestia, Iris, Leto, Asteria, Ganymede, and, since he was widely worshiped as a god, Heracles.<br /> <br /> For the Egyptians, Nephthys (a major figure), Hathor, Sekmet, and Bes, the most widely worshiped God ignored.<br /> <br /> For the Aztecs, Citlalicue (goddess of Female stars) , Toci (healer goddess) and Xochipilli (god of pleasure and fun), The Aztecs need their nicer side.<br /> <br /> For the Norse, just bring some in from the Ragnarok book.<br /> <br /> For the Loas, Oyo (goddess of wind, rain, and lesibans), Oshun (Goddess of Mystery, sweet water, healing, honey, brass, the unknown and unknowable, and dance) and Yemalda (Goddess of the seas, fish, fishing, and mercy.)<br /> <br /> For the Japanese Ame-no-Uzume-Mikoto, (Goddess of the Dawn and Mirth, and the one who can get Amaterasu to act like a grown-up) and Omoikane (as the god of intelligence and wisdom, he's aways needed).<br /> <br /> For the Irish, F\u00f3dla, Creidhne, and Airmed, (they'd add some variety)<br /> <br /> For the Devas, Saraswati, Mariamman, Mitra, and Varuna.<br /> <br /> I don't know the Persian or Chinese gods well enough to ask for individuals.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd like to see Mother Goose, Merlin, and a few other major folkloric figures written up as Scions or Lesser Immortals.<br /> <br /> Note: I forgot the Japanese Goddess of Light and Illusion from Scion companion, Marishen, or something like that. She needs to go in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-21-2017, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T15:19:13-07:00","id":1079533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1079520#post1079520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Greeks, Demeter, Hecate, Hestia, Iris, Leto, Asteria, Ganymede, and, since he was widely worshiped as a god, Heracles.<br /> <br /> For the Egyptians, Nephthys (a major figure), Hathor, Sekmet, and Bes, the most widely worshiped God ignored.<br /> <br /> For the Aztecs, Citlalicue (goddess of Female stars) , Toci (healer goddess) and Xochipilli (god of pleasure and fun), The Aztecs need their nicer side.<br /> <br /> For the Norse, just bring some in from the Ragnarok book.<br /> <br /> For the Loas, Oyo (goddess of wind, rain, and lesibans), Oshun (Goddess of Mystery, sweet water, healing, honey, brass, the unknown and unknowable, and dance) and Yemalda (Goddess of the seas, fish, fishing, and mercy.)<br /> <br /> For the Japanese Ame-no-Uzume-Mikoto, (Goddess of the Dawn and Mirth, and the one who can get Amaterasu to act like a grown-up) and Omoikane (as the god of intelligence and wisdom, he's aways needed).<br /> <br /> For the Irish, F\u00f3dla, Creidhne, and Airmed, (they'd add some variety)<br /> <br /> For the Devas, Saraswati, Mariamman, Mitra, and Varuna.<br /> <br /> I don't know the Persian or Chinese gods well enough to ask for individuals.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd like to see Mother Goose, Merlin, and a few other major folkloric figures written up as Scions or Lesser Immortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demeter, Hestia, Xochipilli and Oya are already confirmed to be in. Also, I'd be <i>really</i> surprised if Sarasvati didn't make the cut. Totally in favour of the other Deva choices though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T15:31:59-07:00","id":1079536,"title":"","content":"Sun Wukong is pretty much guaranteed to be in the Shen, I think it's safe to say.<br /> <br /> \u200bCome to think of it? The Shen have Sun Wukong. The Devas have Hanuman. Is there any connection between the two that we know of? Could we theoretically have TWO trickster monkey gods? Or will one end up being a Mantle of the other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T15:48:59-07:00","id":1079545,"title":"","content":"Nemesis from the Greeks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12529-nico-diangelo","name":"Nico diAngelo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12529_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T17:55:41-07:00","id":1079591,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see Pan, preferably without making him Marsyas and Satan as well. <br /> I'd also like to add my support for the addition of Bes for the Egyptians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T23:41:36-07:00","id":1079699,"title":"","content":"From the Kami Ninigi, and from the Shen Tai Sui Xing and Sui Ren","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","name":"trebius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T23:51:15-07:00","id":1079701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1079536#post1079536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sun Wukong is pretty much guaranteed to be in the Shen, I think it's safe to say.<br /> <br /> \u200bCome to think of it? The Shen have Sun Wukong. The Devas have Hanuman. Is there any connection between the two that we know of? Could we theoretically have TWO trickster monkey gods? Or will one end up being a Mantle of the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's scholarly speculation that Wukong traces his origins back to Hanuman. That said, comparing against the Theoi's Greek and Roman mantles, the equation is more difficult to make, so I'd come down on them being separate in Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:15:50-07:00","id":1079989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1079701#post1079701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's scholarly speculation that Wukong traces his origins back to Hanuman. That said, comparing against the Theoi's Greek and Roman mantles, the equation is more difficult to make, so I'd come down on them being separate in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they're twins?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T10:17:40-07:00","id":1080407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1079989#post1079989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe they're twins?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind, though, that they have very different origins. Sun Wukong crawls from an egg formed of stone, after that stone had been exposed to an exceptional, but natural confluence of subtle forces, including those of wind, sunshine, moonshine, and earthly vapours. Hanuman, meanwhile, is the greatest of a whole people of monkey-men, the Vanaras; he is the son of the wind god Vayu, and the avatar of Shiva. Not that one couldn't fabricate a connection between these two, just to say what you'd be working with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T16:01:23-07:00","id":1080606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1080407#post1080407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind, though, that they have very different origins. Sun Wukong crawls from an egg formed of stone, after that stone had been exposed to an exceptional, but natural confluence of subtle forces, including those of wind, sunshine, moonshine, and earthly vapours. Hanuman, meanwhile, is the greatest of a whole people of monkey-men, the Vanaras; he is the son of the wind god Vayu, and the avatar of Shiva. Not that one couldn't fabricate a connection between these two, just to say what you'd be working with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Sun Wukong is Hanuman's effort to create a son who is as awesome as he is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T23:49:43-07:00","id":1080762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1080606#post1080606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Sun Wukong is Hanuman's effort to create a son who is as awesome as he is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Hanuman did once accidentally create a son when a drop of his perspiration fell into the ocean and somehow impregnated a makara (a crocodile, more or less, just a mythical giant one). That makara was later caught and killed by one of Ravana's many brothers who rules the Terra Incognita of Patala... Said brother mentors him as he grows up and Hanuman later has to fight his own son because of course he does... Though happily he did not die and is in fact made king of that same Terra one Ravana's brother bites it. <br /> <br /> This is one of the metric shitton of extra regional stories that got added to the Ramayana over time, because apparently people thought this epic wasn't long enough already.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The kid's name is Makardhwaja btw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T13:55:27-07:00","id":1081055,"title":"","content":"I will now point to everyone mentioned in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1080635-gods-of-commerce\">Gods of Commerce</a> thread who aren't already included in their pantheon write ups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T13:58:54-07:00","id":1081057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1080762#post1080762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is one of the metric shitton of extra regional stories that got added to the Ramayana over time, because apparently people thought this epic wasn't long enough already.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to get around to reading that one of these days. <br /> <br /> And I now have this image in my head of:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Hanuman: I must fight my son!<br /> Rama: Why?<br /> Hanuman: Because ... Reasons! Shut up!</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T14:35:22-07:00","id":1081083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1081057#post1081057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really need to get around to reading that one of these days.<br /> <br /> And I now have this image in my head of:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Hanuman: I must fight my son!<br /> Rama: Why?<br /> Hanuman: Because ... Reasons! Shut up!</div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, technically, Rama was out cold and about to be turned into a human sacrifice at the time, so I doubt he had any reaction whatsoever <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's why Hanuman was fighting his son in the first place...to get to Rama before Ravana's brother (who is called Mahi Ravana confusingly enough) went all Mola Ram on him.<br /> <br /> Also, my absolute favourite tacked on myth to the Ramayana is the version everyone gets back home after the defeat of Ravana and is celebrating when Sita suddenly says 'Eh, killing Ravana isn't <i>that</i> big a deal...he has an elder brother who's, like, a thousand times more powerful called Sahasta Ravana'. (why all these extra myths love giving Ravana extra brothers is anybody's guess...why all these extra brothers ar also named Ravana only with another word in front is also anybody's guess).<br /> <br /> So Rama and company go to kill this guy (who as far as I can tell has actually not <i>done</i> anything at this point) and they all get knocked out in the first round of combat. So Sita basically goes 'I am surrounded by incompetents' and proceeds to turn into Kali and kill the guy herself. And that is awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> because Sita very desperately needed a version of the story where she is not a damsel in distress. Anyway, Sita-Kali goes on a rampage for kicks, and Brahma and Shiva come over and revive Rama (who, remember, is Vishnu) and the three of them have to grovel a bit before she turns back into Sita <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, if you are interested in reading the Ramayana, I suggest <a href=\"https://archive.org/stream/The.Ramayana.of.Valmiki.by.Hari.Prasad.Shastri#page/n0/mode/2up\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T14:50:33-07:00","id":1081092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1081083#post1081083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Rama and company go to kill this guy (who as far as I can tell has actually not <i>done</i> anything at this point) and they all get knocked out in the first round of combat. So Sita basically goes 'I am surrounded by incompetents' and proceeds to turn into Kali and kill the guy herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm beginning to understand where the plot for Dragon Ball Z originates. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T23:00:32-07:00","id":1081315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1081092#post1081092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I'm beginning to understand where the plot for Dragon Ball Z originates.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually takes a lot more from the &quot;Journey to the West&quot; (&quot;Son Goku&quot; being the Japanese pronounciation of &quot;Sun Wukong&quot; and all that; don't ask me for details, my legitimately only contact with what Dragon Ball is actually about was when I heard some girls talk about it in kindergarten). It's quite astounding, though, how similar the over-the-top fight scenes in those 500-year-old novels are to those we know and love/hate/are weirded out by in modern Eastern media. How much that may be influenced by Indian Epics I can't tell; I haven't heard of Chinese writers taking direct inspiration from Hindu literature, but matters like the Hanuman-Sun Wukong relationship remain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T04:15:32-07:00","id":1081377,"title":"","content":"Hodr, for the norse. Wanted to play a scion of Hodr since watching the almighty johnsons. There is next to no information on him, other than that he was tricked in to killing baldr, but his depiction in the show as being the god of all things cold and dark is awesome. Closest thing I've seen to a god of entropy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T05:22:06-07:00","id":1081393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1081377#post1081377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Closest thing I've seen to a god of entropy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shiva would like a word with you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/originals/78/71/87/787187c98886070dca8cad660d4cdb57.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T14:28:19-07:00","id":1081581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1081377#post1081377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hodr, for the norse. Wanted to play a scion of Hodr since watching the almighty johnsons. There is next to no information on him, other than that he was tricked in to killing baldr, but his depiction in the show as being the god of all things cold and dark is awesome. Closest thing I've seen to a god of entropy.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's Baldr's brother, so I always sort of had the impression that he was meant to be the embodiment of Autumn/Winter and all things associated with it, the way Baldr was the embodiment of Spring/Summer. <br /> <br /> And yes, he'd be a cool addition to the Norse pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T14:30:12-07:00","id":1081582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1081315#post1081315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It actually takes a lot more from the &quot;Journey to the West&quot; (&quot;Son Goku&quot; being the Japanese pronounciation of &quot;Sun Wukong&quot; and all that; don't ask me for details, my legitimately only contact with what Dragon Ball is actually about was when I heard some girls talk about it in kindergarten). It's quite astounding, though, how similar the over-the-top fight scenes in those 500-year-old novels are to those we know and love/hate/are weirded out by in modern Eastern media. How much that may be influenced by Indian Epics I can't tell; I haven't heard of Chinese writers taking direct inspiration from Hindu literature, but matters like the Hanuman-Sun Wukong relationship remain.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would shock me not at all if it turned out that Buddhist missionaries and various traders brought a bunch of those stories into China, which then spread them throughout the rest of Eastern Asia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T22:49:03-07:00","id":1081717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1081582#post1081582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would shock me not at all if it turned out that Buddhist missionaries and various traders brought a bunch of those stories into China, which then spread them throughout the rest of Eastern Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point where it doesn't make sense to me. Because I have never heard of Buddhist missionaries transporting the Epics, which have nothing to do with Buddhism in the slightest, and know of no overt references to those works in China (though I'm of course not a sinologist). Furthermore, the spread of Buddhism to China happens between the 4th and 8th centuries (a time when the Epics were just beginning to be written down), while the &quot;Journey&quot; was written in the 16th; it is <i>about</i> one of the missions to India to retrieve Buddhist scriptures. I've read studies on the formation of Sun Wukong, but they can't really find any mentions of Hanuman as such in the 900 years between the arrival of Buddhism in China and the authoring of the &quot;Journey&quot;; some Chinese monkey demons, though, some of them with Buddhist elements. Ultimately, the contact between India and China was a lot more limited than we tend to imagine, thanks to the Himalayas and several countries being in between (remember that e.g. Tibet was a sovereign empire back then). So, as I said, I can't really tell, because I'm not that much of an expert, but according to all I do know, direct influence seems dubious. The &quot;Journey of the West&quot; isn't generally known as a work that freshly adaptates Indian materials, it's known for introducing Chinese folk traditions (e.g. about blasphemous animal demons) to the higher echelons of literature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T07:07:48-07:00","id":1082245,"title":"","content":"This is one of those things that always made mythology so fascinating to me. When one has two monkey god-heroes in neighboring regions, just what are their connections, if any? Is their some long forgotten proto-monkey god? Is one derived from the other? Or are monkeys just so naturally interesting that it's inevitable that any people living near them will have a monkey god-hero?* One can't help but wonder, for example, if the Japanese Momotaro having a monkey as one of his allies is coincidence or some sort of influence from Journey to the West**?<br /> <br /> Along similar lines, two really weird theories I've heard about Norse mythology: One, that Freyja is just Freyr cross dressing as part of some sort of shamanic seidr ritual activity; Two, that Baldr is actually derived from stories of Jesus as they made their way up through Germany and into Scandinavia during the first millennium. Not that I'm actually sold on either of them. I just find them interesting thought-fodder. <br /> <br /> *<sub>Given the huge number of primate characters in comic books, I'm inclined toward the idea that monkeys just make for fun stories. </sub><br /> **<sub>Also, if you've never seen Stephen Chow's version of Journey to the West, it's wonderfully awesome and great Scion inspiration. </sub>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T20:14:51-07:00","id":1082496,"title":"","content":"It's unfortunate we don't have more information on the religions of pre-Christian Europe. I know that such mergings and accumulations can be seen in religions where more historical/archaeological evidence exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:54:41-07:00","id":1115268,"title":"","content":"The faery queens of Ireland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T20:14:51-07:00","id":1115344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1068121#post1068121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The minors greeks gods (nike, hypno, morpheo etcetc)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Don't forget Trivia, Roman goddess of witchcraft and sorcery.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:09:58-07:00","id":1115372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1115344#post1115344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Don't forget Trivia, Roman goddess of witchcraft and sorcery.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bPretty sure Hecate's got that one locked down, seeing as how she's much more well-known. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:49:05-07:00","id":1115386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1115372#post1115372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bPretty sure Hecate's got that one locked down, seeing as how she's much more well-known. </div> </div> </div> </div>Mantles, people! They exist for a reason!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T08:09:54-07:00","id":1115532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1115372#post1115372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bPretty sure Hecate's got that one locked down, seeing as how she's much more well-known.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trivia was strongly identified with Hecate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T16:29:55-07:00","id":1115712,"title":"","content":"Going by people I think are major gods, I have some additions planned out. Ignoring the pantheons that we haven't seen yet, my additions would be...<br /> <br /> For the Theoi<br /> Definitely Pan.<br /> Maybe Hecate (but she's technically a Titan), Janus (hard to come up with associations) and Quirinus (has no post-apotheosis myths).<br /> <br /> For the Tuatha<br /> Definitely Goibniu<br /> Maybe Flidais. She's cool and has a few myths, but I'm not sure<br /> <br /> For the Teotl<br /> Definitely Tlazolteotl.<br /> <br /> For the Netjer<br /> Definitely Nephthys and Sekhmet<br /> Maybe Bes and Neith. Bes is super popular but has no myths, and Neith is definitely a major goddess, but her ancient nature has me considering her a possible Titan.<br /> <br /> For the Shen<br /> Definitely Houyi and definitely making Xiwangmu a goddess<br /> Maybe Yu Huang. Even though he has the makings for a primordial, many stories do have the Jade Emperor as a former mortal and clearly differentiate him from Yuanshi Tianzun and Shangdi, so it really depends on which myths I go with.<br /> <br /> For the Orisha<br /> Maybe Erinle and Olokun, need to do more research on them though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13472,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","user":"~NKF~","date":".  Now that we have the revised Netjer and know Nephthys and Sekhmet don't have writeups, I fully intend to do writeups for them eventually. 08-05-2017, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T22:04:41-07:00","id":1115795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~NKF~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1115712#post1115712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by people I think are major gods, I have some additions planned out. Ignoring the pantheons that we haven't seen yet, my additions would be...<br /> <br /> For the Theoi<br /> Definitely Pan.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I too would support the idea of them incorporating Pan, but this time NOT make him literally Satan.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I get agitated enough when people keep depicting Hades as the villain and focus exclusively on Tartarus when depicting the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T22:39:49-07:00","id":1115808,"title":"","content":"Yeah, of the previewed pantheons only the Tuatha de Danann don't have someone that I believe really warrents inclusion as a major divinity (and that's only because I assume Goibniu is still hanging around the Nemetondevos like in 1e).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T05:02:26-07:00","id":1115885,"title":"","content":"I can see keeping Goibniu (as Gobannos) in the Nemetondevos, but in truth, he plays a massive role in Irish Myths so I'd rather keep him in the pantheon where he actually has stories, rather than one where he's mostly just a name on a few inscriptions and a couple statues. Of course, he could be in both with mantles being a thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yeah, Pan being the devil makes no sense to me. There are countless gods Christians compared to the devil (Ba'al, Chernobog, Loki, Hades, Cernunnos, Eshu, Ordog etc.) so there's really no reason to make Pan the devil in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T05:57:11-07:00","id":1115902,"title":"","content":"I'll join NKF in supporting Bes. That guy was insanely popular. It's said that he was the original inspiration for the whole gargoyle concept that countless other cultures adopted. &quot;Put up a scary statue and it will scare away evil?&quot; Yeah. That was pretty much Bes. His worship was EVERYWHERE in the Ancient World. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:25:54-07:00","id":1115917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1115902#post1115902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll join NKF in supporting Bes. That guy was insanely popular. It's said that he was the original inspiration for the whole gargoyle concept that countless other cultures adopted. &quot;Put up a scary statue and it will scare away evil?&quot; Yeah. That was pretty much Bes. His worship was EVERYWHERE in the Ancient World.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought the &quot;scary face that scares off evil&quot; concept came first, then people started assigning names to it. Rather than a specific god's worship spreading across the entire globe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, we <i>are </i>going to see gods without Pantheons, right? Read that somewhere quite some time ago, so not sure if that's still the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T07:05:00-07:00","id":1115931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~NKF~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1115885#post1115885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see keeping Goibniu (as Gobannos) in the Nemetondevos, but in truth, he plays a massive role in Irish Myths so I'd rather keep him in the pantheon where he actually has stories, rather than one where he's mostly just a name on a few inscriptions and a couple statues. Of course, he could be in both with mantles being a thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yeah, Pan being the devil makes no sense to me. There are countless gods Christians compared to the devil (Ba'al, Chernobog, Loki, Hades, Cernunnos, Eshu, Ordog etc.) so there's really no reason to make Pan the devil in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Especially since Pan was a god of love. If they wanted a Satanic figure, they should have gone with Loki, who's entire shtick is that he screws with people for his own amusement and eventually brings about the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Although I hear that 2e will try to move away from depicting characters as other religious icons. It was pretty obvious that Aten was supposed to be the Judeo Christian god in 1e, which meant anybody belonging to the Abrahamic faiths were unwittingly part of a global Titan cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T08:44:01-07:00","id":1115956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1115931#post1115931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although I hear that 2e will try to move away from depicting characters as other religious icons. It was pretty obvious that Aten was supposed to be the Judeo Christian god in 1e, which meant anybody belonging to the Abrahamic faiths were unwittingly part of a global Titan cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was \u2026 not good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, it might be interesting to explore the idea of, for example, Catholic &quot;Scions&quot; who have divine power but instead of an actual blood parent have an Angel or Saint as a patron. (This may also work for Buddhists, but I'm not enough of an expert on that faith to say.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T12:17:10-07:00","id":1116051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1115956#post1115956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that was \u2026 not good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, it might be interesting to explore the idea of, for example, Catholic &quot;Scions&quot; who have divine power but instead of an actual blood parent have an Angel or Saint as a patron. (This may also work for Buddhists, but I'm not enough of an expert on that faith to say.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, in Catholicism, the saints are recognized as people who can channel God's power through themselves in order to perform miracles. So it wouldn't be too difficult for an ST to rework Scions to function in a similar capacity. The question is how far each Scion would / should be allowed to progress in their adventurers, since the Abrahamic faiths refuse to acknowledge the legitimacy of any deity beyond their own.<br /> <br /> Long ago, they used to be polytheistic, complete with a pantheon of different gods and goddesses. Over time, this pantheon was changed to the point where each of the individual deities was considered to be an avatar of a singular, all powerful being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-14-2017, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T13:45:20-07:00","id":1116538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1116051#post1116051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, in Catholicism, the saints are recognized as people who can channel God's power through themselves in order to perform miracles. So it wouldn't be too difficult for an ST to rework Scions to function in a similar capacity. The question is how far each Scion would / should be allowed to progress in their adventurers, since the Abrahamic faiths refuse to acknowledge the legitimacy of any deity beyond their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. At a guess, if one reached &quot;God&quot; status, they'd be the equivalent of one of the major league Saints like St. Peter, the Apostle Paul or John the Baptist, maybe?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T13:47:51-07:00","id":1118687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~NKF~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1115885#post1115885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see keeping Goibniu (as Gobannos) in the Nemetondevos, but in truth, he plays a massive role in Irish Myths so I'd rather keep him in the pantheon where he actually has stories, rather than one where he's mostly just a name on a few inscriptions and a couple statues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, that's every Gaulish god. But don't worry, it's looking like you'll get the smith god that you know and love in at least one form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~NKF~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1115885#post1115885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, he could be in both with mantles being a thing</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, using the same mantle to be a member of two pantheons is also a thing. But it's... stressful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T16:07:12-07:00","id":1118740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arlecchino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1118687#post1118687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly, that's every Gaulish god. But don't worry, it's looking like you'll get the smith god that you know and love in at least one form.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As I understand it, using the same mantle to be a member of two pantheons is also a thing. But it's... stressful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm aware. But unlike folks like Sukellos, Rosmerta, Sirona and Esus, Gobannos has a very clear Irish and Welsh equivalent, so I feel it makes more sense to include him as Goibniu or Gofannon who actually have myths and stories to go on for his write-up, whereas Gobannos has the fact that Romans compared him to Vulcan and a few short inscriptions to go on. Plus, last I heard, the Nemetondevos are being treated as a &quot;dead&quot; pantheon, so it just makes sense for folks like Lugus and Gobannos to leave to other pantheons rather than stick around. But again, all that's my opinion obviously.<br /> <br /> But yeah, with mantles, Goibniu, Gofannon and Gobannos could all potentially be included, so we'll have to wait and see what goes down. Overall, my list was just saying who I personally will do unofficial write-ups for if they don't get official ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T17:47:58-07:00","id":1129504,"title":"","content":"Where would Cybele/Magna Mater fit in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T18:10:41-07:00","id":1129526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1129504#post1129504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where would Cybele/Magna Mater fit in?</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is same being as the non-hostile Titan Rhea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T22:06:25-07:00","id":1129676,"title":"","content":"Was anything ever said about if Hecate is in the book or not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T22:10:40-07:00","id":1129680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1129676#post1129676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was anything ever said about if Hecate is in the book or not?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't believe she made the list for the core (12 Olympians + Hades, Hestia, &amp; Persephone, last we saw). That's already pushing above what was going to be the cap.<br /> <br /> Were I to pick 2 Theoi to use as examples of &quot;additional gods&quot; for the Companion, it would be Pan &amp; Hecate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T22:18:18-07:00","id":1129683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1129680#post1129680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't believe she made the list for the core (12 Olympians + Hades, Hestia, &amp; Persephone, last we saw). That's already pushing above what was going to be the cap.<br /> <br /> Were I to pick 2 Theoi to use as examples of &amp;quot;additional gods&amp;quot; for the Companion, it would be Pan &amp; Hecate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd hope she'd go in the Companion and not tucked away in a hypothetical Titans and Titanspawn book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T22:20:37-07:00","id":1129684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1129683#post1129683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd hope she'd go in the Companion and not tucked away in a hypothetical Titans and Titanspawn book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I remember Neall saying cases like her and Iris would be handled as goddesses, with &quot;Titan&quot; being more a political label about their background, rather than a hard and fast metaphysical category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T01:15:23-07:00","id":1129712,"title":"","content":"I don't expect the gameline to do it because of spacing reasons, but I'd love to see an interesting, creative writeup for Hekate. The kind that does a good job of mixing up the mythological character with creative reimagining would be fabulous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T09:25:11-07:00","id":1133828,"title":"","content":"I am surprised that Annansi isn't already in the Orisha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T09:30:56-07:00","id":1133829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1133828#post1133828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am surprised that Annansi isn't already in the Orisha.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be because Anansi isn't actually one of the Orisha! The Orisha are the Pantheon of the Yoruban culture, while Anansi is a figure from a different cultural group which is best known for the Ashanti Empire. They have a very different religious system from the Yoruban peoples to their south, and are semi-Monotheistic with an Supreme God named Nyame, assisted by a host of other supernatural entities called Abossom.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, Anansi <i>isn't</i> a Deity, he isn't worshiped by the Ashanti, but he is involved in some versions of the creation myth, and is heavily involved in the folkloric Spider Stories. There is more than enough figures in the Pantheon of the Ashanti however to put together a nice Pantheon for Anansi to hang out in though! Myself and Sacerdos have done a bunch of research for them, and have some rough drafts of the Pantheon finished. They are a <i>really cool</i> group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T09:38:45-07:00","id":1133833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1133828#post1133828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am surprised that Annansi isn't already in the Orisha.</div> </div> </div> </div>He doesn't share their origin, for one thing - they're Yoruba, he's Ashanti. And while he's a part of Caribbean folklore, he's not considered part of the Loa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T12:49:45-07:00","id":1133915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1133829#post1133829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be because Anansi isn't actually one of the Orisha! The Orisha are the Pantheon of the Yoruban culture, while Anansi is a figure from a different cultural group which is best known for the Ashanti Empire. They have a very different religious system from the Yoruban peoples to their south, and are semi-Monotheistic with an Supreme God named Nyame, assisted by a host of other supernatural entities called Abossom.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, Anansi <i>isn't</i> a Deity, he isn't worshiped by the Ashanti, but he is involved in some versions of the creation myth, and is heavily involved in the folkloric Spider Stories. There is more than enough figures in the Pantheon of the Ashanti however to put together a nice Pantheon for Anansi to hang out in though! Myself and Sacerdos have done a bunch of research for them, and have some rough drafts of the Pantheon finished. They are a <i>really cool</i> group.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no evidence Loki was a worshipped deity either, but he clearly plays the narrative role of a divinity in Norse myths. So as Scion's about myth and not religion, Anansi still strongly fits into the divinity role as a trickster culture hero child of higher divinities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T13:48:00-07:00","id":1133934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1133915#post1133915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no evidence Loki was a worshipped deity either, but he clearly plays the narrative role of a divinity in Norse myths. So as Scion's about myth and not religion, Anansi still strongly fits into the divinity role as a trickster culture hero child of higher divinities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I think I didn't explain myself well enough! Yeah, we don't have any evidence of Loki being worshiped, or Lugh, but Anansi is specifically <i>not</i> worshiped by the Ashanti. Their religious system has never died out, their King, Osei Tutu II, is still a Divine Monarch, he rules with the will of Nyame through the Golden Stool. The Abosom are still worshiped, their ancestral spirits are still worshiped, Nyame, and Asase Ya are still worshiped. But Anansi, <i>very specifically</i>, is not.<br /> <br /> So, for sure, Anansi will make an awesome Divine Parent, but he's not a God. Like, in the strict sense, not in the 'gameplay' sense. The Abosom probably don't like him very much, his role in the stories is a &quot;And this is why you shouldn't be a bad person, look what happens to Anansi,&quot; sort of thing. But he'd be a totally viable Divine Parent. His cultural group just doesn't regard him as a God. Never was, and still isn't. So, when we get the Abosom all written up, Anansi will totally be a Divine Parent option, but the Abosom don't consider him to be a God. He's a weird... other thing.<br /> <br /> Technically, none of the Abosom are Gods, only Nyame is. But, Anansi is specifically <i>not</i> one of the Abosom, the beings who fill the role of 'Gods' in other cultures. Anansi's just his own thing. Very powerful, creaiton-myth powerful, tricking an all-seeing, all-knowing (sorta, it's tricky), all-powerful God powerful. But, technically not an Abosom.<br /> <br /> We just really feel like it's important to make note of the difference to be respectful to the Ashanti people since it's a living religion. It'll make more sense when we post the entire thing for sure, I have written a big long section on the Nature of Divinity for the Ashanti since it's a bit tricky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T13:59:06-07:00","id":1133939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1133829#post1133829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be because Anansi isn't actually one of the Orisha! The Orisha are the Pantheon of the Yoruban culture, while Anansi is a figure from a different cultural group which is best known for the Ashanti Empire. They have a very different religious system from the Yoruban peoples to their south, and are semi-Monotheistic with an Supreme God named Nyame, assisted by a host of other supernatural entities called Abossom.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, Anansi <i>isn't</i> a Deity, he isn't worshiped by the Ashanti, but he is involved in some versions of the creation myth, and is heavily involved in the folkloric Spider Stories. There is more than enough figures in the Pantheon of the Ashanti however to put together a nice Pantheon for Anansi to hang out in though! Myself and Sacerdos have done a bunch of research for them, and have some rough drafts of the Pantheon finished. They are a <i>really cool</i> group.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you! I didn't know this at all and now I'm looking up more stuff!<br /> <br /> So then, I amend my statement: I'd love to see the Abosom in 2nd Ed. (and hopefully Anansi somewhere in there) ^.^<br /> <br /> EDIT: Watcher, are you one of the devs? As in, is this a confirmation that the Abosom are going to be in 2nd Ed? Or is this a fan supplement? <br /> <br /> The 'We' statements have me wondering ^.^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 08-25-2017, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T14:30:35-07:00","id":1133948,"title":"","content":"For the Kami, I'd like to see Ama-no-Uzume, Tenjin, Takemikazuchi, and Konohana Sakuya added to the roster (and if her sister is there, Iha-Naga probably should be too). I'd also kinda like to see Tsukuyomi retained (largely for sentimental reasons) as an option for a dIvine parent.<br /> <br /> For the Aesir, I'd like to see Forseti and Idun included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T15:04:31-07:00","id":1133954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1133934#post1133934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I think I didn't explain myself well enough! Yeah, we don't have any evidence of Loki being worshiped, or Lugh, but Anansi is specifically <i>not</i> worshiped by the Ashanti. Their religious system has never died out, their King, Osei Tutu II, is still a Divine Monarch, he rules with the will of Nyame through the Golden Stool. The Abosom are still worshiped, their ancestral spirits are still worshiped, Nyame, and Asase Ya are still worshiped. But Anansi, <i>very specifically</i>, is not.<br /> <br /> So, for sure, Anansi will make an awesome Divine Parent, but he's not a God. Like, in the strict sense, not in the 'gameplay' sense. The Abosom probably don't like him very much, his role in the stories is a &amp;quot;And this is why you shouldn't be a bad person, look what happens to Anansi,&amp;quot; sort of thing. But he'd be a totally viable Divine Parent. His cultural group just doesn't regard him as a God. Never was, and still isn't. So, when we get the Abosom all written up, Anansi will totally be a Divine Parent option, but the Abosom don't consider him to be a God. He's a weird... other thing.<br /> <br /> Technically, none of the Abosom are Gods, only Nyame is. But, Anansi is specifically <i>not</i> one of the Abosom, the beings who fill the role of 'Gods' in other cultures. Anansi's just his own thing. Very powerful, creaiton-myth powerful, tricking an all-seeing, all-knowing (sorta, it's tricky), all-powerful God powerful. But, technically not an Abosom.<br /> <br /> We just really feel like it's important to make note of the difference to be respectful to the Ashanti people since it's a living religion. It'll make more sense when we post the entire thing for sure, I have written a big long section on the Nature of Divinity for the Ashanti since it's a bit tricky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, didn't mean to suggest that Ashanti beliefs are dead or reconstructed as opposed to continuously alive! I just meant that there's precedent for treating someone who isn't a worshipped god as a viable divine parent within a pantheon.<br /> <br /> Your research on the Abosom and Ashanti traditions has been fantastic Watcher and your contribution on the African Pantheons thread definitely convinced me at least that there's enough material for a full Pantheon (my previous opinion having been that the Ashanti being largely monotheistic, the best course was to treat Nyame and Asase Ye as primordials and Anansi as a roving demigod without a broader Pantheon, but you turned me around!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T20:24:05-07:00","id":1134030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1133939#post1133939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! I didn't know this at all and now I'm looking up more stuff!<br /> <br /> So then, I amend my statement: I'd love to see the Abosom in 2nd Ed. (and hopefully Anansi somewhere in there) ^.^<br /> <br /> EDIT: Watcher, are you one of the devs? As in, is this a confirmation that the Abosom are going to be in 2nd Ed? Or is this a fan supplement?<br /> <br /> The 'We' statements have me wondering ^.^</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ashanti are a <i>really cool</i> cultural group, and their religious system is so neat. I think they would be a wonderful addition to anyone's game, and I really love the idea of being able to help flesh Africa out some more.<br /> <br /> And no, I am not one of the Devs, I'm sorry if I mislead you Xiongrey! I spend a lot of time working on houseruled Pantheons for Scion along with some friends of mine, though I have been sitting on my research for over a year now waiting for Scion 2e to come out. My friends and myself have put together <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/home\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> houseruled project, though my revision for the Kami which I completed thanks to the invaluable help of my good friend Sacerdos is my new standard for Pantheons. If you want to get a feel for what the Hittites, Ashanti, and Haida will be like, check them out <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nn03gHFj_tgASkDPGbI1FgtTBff88OrgioSJzyIvEbY/edit\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> I am a historian, and I am doing a MA in Celtic Studies, so this sort of thing is my passion. I have been playing Scion since high school, so I like doing these projects both as a form of relaxation, and also to give back to the community. When I say 'We,' I mean Iry, Aynie, Sacerdos, and myself. The people who work on the Scion 2.0 rules, and help me put together these Pantheons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1133954#post1133954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, didn't mean to suggest that Ashanti beliefs are dead or reconstructed as opposed to continuously alive! I just meant that there's precedent for treating someone who isn't a worshipped god as a viable divine parent within a pantheon.<br /> <br /> Your research on the Abosom and Ashanti traditions has been fantastic Watcher and your contribution on the African Pantheons thread definitely convinced me at least that there's enough material for a full Pantheon (my previous opinion having been that the Ashanti being largely monotheistic, the best course was to treat Nyame and Asase Ye as primordials and Anansi as a roving demigod without a broader Pantheon, but you turned me around!)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really sorry if that came off as sounding harsh Glamourweaver! I am really anxious about not screwing the Haida and Ashanti up, I dread dropping the ball on them. I am desperate for there to be more representation from First Nations cultural groups, as well as Africa for Scion. But, at the same time, I'm spending a lot of time making sure I am not screwing things up somehow, and that the myths I am using were collected with the permissions of people who belonged to those cultural groups.<br /> <br /> You're absolutely right there is precedent for treating someone as a Divine Parent who doesn't have worship! Heck, Xhuuya from the Haida Pantheon (better known to english speaking audiences as Raven) doesn't get worshiped, and wasn't worshiped by the Haida either according to the historical interviews and ethnographies I have read. The way it is described is that 'he takes too much and gives too little.' The relationship the Haida have with their Supernatural Beings is so neat, I can't wait to show it off. I'm sorry for jumping down your throat there, I know you're a really awesome person Glamourweaver, I am sorry for going full-on there.<br /> <br /> But, I am really glad you have been enjoying seeing me blather about the Abosom and the Ashanti! They are so, so cool. I am just so excited to give you all these Pantheons, I think they will really add to people's games. I also hope they will help educate people in the history, and traditions of these groups. They are just so interesting, I have learned so much researching them, and I hope that other people will enjoy them just as much as I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 08-26-2017, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T21:35:38-07:00","id":1134043,"title":"","content":"I was somehow under the impression that the Haida raven was named Nankil'slas. Was I misinformed, or do they have two ravens? Or one with two names?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T22:50:48-07:00","id":1134058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1134043#post1134043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was somehow under the impression that the Haida raven was named Nankil'slas. Was I misinformed, or do they have two ravens? Or one with two names?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolute ton of names! Like, so many. Names have a special position in Haida culture, more names, more important, that sort of thing in basic. It is really interesting. NA\u00f1k\u00ee\u2019lsLas is a name that Xhuuya goes by during the very end of the creation myth. I tend to refer to him as Xhuuya since it is his first name, and because NA\u00f1k\u00ee\u2019lsLas is the problem-entity I eluded to at the end there. There might be another person called NA\u00f1k\u00ee\u2019lsLas, or Xhuuya might also be that person, but in that case he was two different people at once, one of whom didn't realize he was the same person, and he was his own heir, except the other Supernatural Beings respect the elder-NA\u00f1k\u00ee\u2019lsLas more than they do Xhuuya-NA\u00f1k\u00ee\u2019lsLas which suggests they might not be the same person? (Another edit for clarity here. While this sort of thing may sound standard for mythology, people having multiple bodies, it's unprecedented in Haida myth, and the section where it comes up is <i>super</i> unclear in the different translations I have read.)<br /> <br /> It's... really confusing, and there doesn't seem to be any real consensus internally. It's my current 'thing' I'm fiddling with and trying to research. Not much luck sadly.<br /> <br /> (If you are interested in Xhuuya's other names, here is a list! NA\u00f1k\u00ee\u2019lsLas (Nang Kilstlas, translated as Voicehandler) Nang Kilstlas Hlingaay (translated as Voicehandler\u2019s Heir), Xhuuya (translated as Raven), The One We Speak Of (the Haida don't always give Xhuuya a name since the general consensus is he doesn't deserve the names he has. He isn't... seen in a very good light), and W\u012b\u2019g\u00eet.)<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, and if anyone would like to read some Haida mythology, check out A<i> Story As Sharp As A Knife: The Classical Haida Mythtellers And Their World</i>, and <i>Nine Visits to the Mythworld</i>, both collections of traditional oral accounts from the turn of the 20th century, recorded with permission, and translated by Robert Bringhurst. Lovely reads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 08-26-2017, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T21:09:41-07:00","id":1134742,"title":"","content":"If i had to pick 1 per Pantheon we've seen so far, I think it would have to be...<br /> <br /> - Pan for the Theoi (Hecate is also very close, but I think Pan might get more gameplay use via his tie to the Satyrs)<br /> - Neber-Het for the Netjer (pretty much a must, given that she's the missing member of the Psedjet/Ennead of Heliopolis)<br /> - Goibnu for the Tuatha<br /> - Oba for the Orisha<br /> - Tlazolteotl for the Teotl<br /> - Caishen for the Shen<br /> <br /> Obviously can't comment on the Aesir, Kami, Deva, or Manitou until they're previewed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T23:58:09-07:00","id":1134767,"title":"","content":"Weren't the Aesir already Previewed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T00:05:20-07:00","id":1134769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1134767#post1134767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't the Aesir already Previewed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Were they? I missed it/forgot if so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T00:09:55-07:00","id":1134772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1134769#post1134769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Were they? I missed it/forgot if so.</div> </div> </div> </div>They weren't. Got a bit in the alpha slice, but I think that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T00:28:00-07:00","id":1135694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1067714-which-gods-and-goddesses-do-you-want-added-to-existing-pantheons?p=1134742#post1134742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Pan for the Theoi (Hecate is also very close, but I think Pan might get more gameplay use via his tie to the Satyrs)</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, if a distinctly Roman sub-pantheon isn't getting a full writeup, Janus would work as the Theoi's additional member. He is pretty much the most important Roman god without a Greek counterpart, with standing on par with the major Olympians' counterparts in Roman worship.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm thinking Fortune, Journeys, Prosperity, Stars (assuming its still the time purview), &amp; War<br /> <br /> Liminal, Guardian... and I'm not sure on the third Calling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-01-2017, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T22:51:36-07:00","id":1136837,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it - given Plutarch's story of the death of Pan being proclaimed in the first century during the reign of Tiberius, Pan might be a good choice of an Incarnate character (particularly a Satyr).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}